<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">626 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">626 CE in world history: 5 events, 1 birth and 3 deaths. 252 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/552">552 CE</a><a href="/years/554">554 CE</a><a href="/years/602">602 CE</a><a href="/years/618">618 CE</a><a href="/years/626" aria-current="page">626 CE</a><a href="/years/627">627 CE</a><a href="/years/628">628 CE</a><a href="/years/630">630 CE</a><a href="/years/632">632 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-29">29 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Avars and Persians begin their assault on Constantinople</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 80,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>, allied with the Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>, began a coordinated assault on the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, defended by some 12,000 Byzantine troops. After a month of bombardment, with their fleets sunk, the attackers abandoned the siege.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/xuanwu-gate-incident" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xuanwu-gate-incident.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-2">2 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Li Shimin kills his brothers in the Xuanwu Gate Incident</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a> ambushed and killed his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-jiancheng">Li Jiancheng</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-yuanji">Li Yuanji</a> at the Xuanwu Gate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>. Within two months his father abdicated, and as Emperor Taizong he presided over a golden age of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanwu-gate-incident">Xuanwu Gate Incident</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-jiancheng">Li Jiancheng</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-4">4 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Li Shimin takes the Tang throne as Emperor Taizong</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a>, who had encouraged his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang">Li Yuan</a>'s rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a>, took the throne as the second Tang emperor, known after his death as Taizong. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-turkic-khaganate">Eastern Turkic Khaganate</a> and extended Tang power into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Emperor Taizong of Tang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
